# Docker and tooling

**All project runtime goes through `docker/run.sh`.** That includes CPU-only
tests, one-liners, imports, train, eval, and diagnostics. Host `python` /
`python3` / `/usr/bin/python` / a host venv / `uv run` are wrong even for a
"quick" test. Git itself stays on the host. Full notes: `docs/docker_usage.md`.

```bash
# ❌ BAD  (system Python, missing torch/swm, wrong GL)
python scripts/test_smear_structure.py
python3 -c "import torch"

# ✅ GOOD  (from docker/)
./run.sh python scripts/test_smear_structure.py
./run.sh python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())"
```

## Why run.sh

Compose service `lewm` has `container_name: weltmodelle-lewm`. `docker compose
run` creates a **second** container and fights that name. `run.sh` starts the
named one if needed, `compose exec`s, and stops it only if **this** invocation
started it.

```bash
cd docker
./run.sh up --build    # first time, or after Dockerfile changes
./run.sh               # start if needed, bash, then graceful stop
./run.sh python …      # start if needed, command, then stop if we started it
./run.sh up            # leave running until stop / host shutdown
./run.sh stop          # SIGTERM, 30s grace; container object remains
```

If already up via `./run.sh up`, a later `./run.sh python …` does **not** stop
it — call `./run.sh stop` when finished. No restart-on-boot.

Image `weltmodelle-lewm:local`: CUDA 12.6, Python 3.10, torch cu126,
`stable-worldmodel[train,env]`. Startup does not pip.

## Bind mounts (the only filesystem)

Compose bind is `..:/workspace` from `docker/`, so **this clone (or sibling
worktree) is `/workspace`**. There are **no** named/anonymous Docker volumes.
Edits and `eval_results/` on either side are the same files. Stop/reboot keep
host data. `/opt/venv` is **in the image**, not mounted.

| Host (this tree) | In container | Notes |
|------------------|--------------|--------|
| `<this-ws_weltmodelle>/` | `/workspace` | Whole workspace; compose `..:/workspace` |
| `ws_le-wm/le-wm/` | `/workspace/ws_le-wm/le-wm` | **cwd**. Scripts, `eval_results/`, configs |
| `ws_le-wm/docs/` | `/workspace/ws_le-wm/docs` | Research docs (parent git, not the submodule) |
| `ws_le-wm/stablewm/` | `/workspace/ws_le-wm/stablewm` | `$STABLEWM_HOME` (ckpts, HDF5; gitignored caches) |
| `docker/` | `/workspace/docker` | Dockerfile, `run.sh`, compose |
| `docker/home/` | `/workspace/docker/home` | `$HOME` (dotfiles, caches; not `~` on the host) |
| `docs/` | `/workspace/docs` | Workspace how-tos |
| — | `/opt/venv` | Image Python; **not** a host path. Never `le-wm/.venv` |
| `/tmp/.X11-unix` | `/tmp/.X11-unix` | Host X for GLFW viewers |

A sibling worktree is a different `/workspace`: run **that** tree’s
`docker/run.sh`. Do not assume the main clone’s files unless they are the
same bind.

`compose exec` skips the entrypoint; compose sets `PATH` to `/opt/venv/bin`.

Torch/CEM use the NVIDIA GPU. MuJoCo/PushT: **EGL** offscreen, **GLFW** on the
host X (Intel). Do not set `__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia`.

## Do not

- Create `ws_le-wm/le-wm/.venv` (or `docker/.venv`) on the host.
- `pip` / `uv pip` on the host to "set up" the project.
- `docker compose down` unless you mean to delete the container (image + host
  files stay). Don't `up --build` every session.
- Install packages into a running container as the source of truth — edit
  `docker/Dockerfile` and `./run.sh up --build` once.

## How to run code

From `docker/` (cwd inside the container is already `le-wm/`):

```bash
./run.sh python eval_live.py --env pusht --episodes 1 --no-video
./run.sh python scripts/test_smear_structure.py
./run.sh python train.py data=pusht          # upstream HDF5 train; rare here
```

Tests are `scripts/test_*.py` with a `__main__` runner. Invoke them as
`./run.sh python scripts/test_foo.py` from `docker/` — not a host pytest
suite and not system Python. Needs NVIDIA driver + nvidia-container-toolkit.
